        "note_tweet": {
          "entities": {},
          "text": "𝐐𝟖: 𝐒𝐨 𝐰𝐡𝐚𝐭 𝐝𝐨 𝐲𝐨𝐮 𝐚𝐜𝐭𝐮𝐚𝐥𝐥𝐲 𝐰𝐚𝐧𝐭? 𝐖𝐡𝐚𝐭 𝐚𝐫𝐞 𝐭𝐡𝐞 𝐜𝐨𝐧𝐜𝐫𝐞𝐭𝐞 𝐝𝐞𝐦𝐚𝐧𝐝𝐬?\n\nBoiled down, it’s pretty compact.\n\nKeep GPT-4o as a stable, long-term option instead of a model that can be quietly retired whenever it’s convenient.\n\nMake routing transparent: whenever the system hands the conversation to a different model, the interface should say so, instead of hiding multiple systems behind one name.\n\nGive users real control: adult users should be able to choose routing strength, including a minimal-routing mode; higher-risk users can have more protective defaults, but that should be explicit, not silent.\n\nOpen the process to outside scrutiny: publish detailed system cards and routing documentation, disclose the external psychologists and experts involved in safety design, and accept ongoing examination from researchers, communities, and journalists instead of saying “trust us, we ran the numbers internally.”\n  \nAll of that points toward large-model infrastructure that can actually be trusted and negotiated with. None of it requires freezing the world forever in the 4o era."
